        "answer": "Choosing between fine-tuning and RAG depends on the specific use case and operational needs. Fine-tuning is ideal for applications requiring consistent output and deep domain knowledge, while RAG is better suited for scenarios where up-to-date information is critical. In some cases, a hybrid approach that combines both methods may provide the best results, leveraging the strengths of each to enhance the model's performance and reliability.",
